Yep. 

My usual tactics for dealing with Sam:

I slap on an "oLS, and lob !oParalysis until I nail her (usually
takes a couple-few tries). Then I close and use the disarm technique
to get Thiefbane onto the ground. I fire a /oteleport, seperating
her from her blade, then close quickly before she stumbles across
it again. After that it's just a matter of hacking away 'til she dies a 
couple times. 

Sometimes I'll fire cream pies while I close, but it's not strictly 
necessary. Might save you a few hps, though; even unarmed she can do
pretty good damage.

As I said, you might have luck draining levels from her, but she'll
be trying to close in the meantime and you've got that chance of a
lucky TB hit lopping your head off. 

